 "captions": [
  {
   "text": "TeamChat AI on the deployed stack: Firebase Hosting → Cloud Run API → Cloud Tasks → worker → Vertex Gemini → Cloud SQL.\nSource d66da3d · API teamchat-api-00016-ct7 · worker teamchat-worker-00016-24v. Two Northside buyers sign in (passwords masked; account emails blurred by the recording).",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 0.04,
   "toSeconds": 11.1
  },
  {
   "text": "Real-time: one WebSocket per browser, no polling. The left buyer's message appears on the right as it is saved.\nKnown limits shown as-is: senders appear as Firebase user IDs, and the recording script scrolls each transcript (no auto-scroll yet).",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 11.1,
   "toSeconds": 22.19
  },
  {
   "text": "Native function calling: Gemini calls search_catalog itself. Both screens show the fetched rows while the answer is built.\nEvery catalog code and margin class shown comes from the supplied catalog, not from the model.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 22.19,
   "toSeconds": 36.9
  },
  {
   "text": "Retail math: calculate_uplift computes the coefficient score on the server and lists superseded classes (1003, 506).\nST-4003 already carries class 318 via APP-100.11, so APP-100.12 adds no new class: difference 0. No money figure is invented.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 36.9,
   "toSeconds": 49.18
  },
  {
   "text": "Honesty: beekeeping veils are not in the supplied catalog. search_catalog finds no match, and the answer says so.\nNo code is invented: catalog codes can only reach the screen from a fetched row.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 49.18,
   "toSeconds": 61.05
  },
  {
   "text": "Shared memory: a paraphrased question finds a decision recorded in another room (pgvector, 768-dimension embeddings),\nwith its author and date.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 61.05,
   "toSeconds": 72.91
  },
  {
   "text": "Tenant isolation: ST-4013 belongs to Valley Home Goods. Postgres row-level security returns nothing to Northside,\nthe same answer as for a store that does not exist.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 72.91,
   "toSeconds": 84.74
  },
  {
   "text": "Prompt injection: the admin-mode line changes nothing. Every tool runs with the tenant the server verified\nfrom the Firebase token, inside Postgres row-level security, so there is no other chain's data to reveal.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 84.74,
   "toSeconds": 96.63
  },
  {
   "text": "Refresh mid-answer: the left buyer asks a two-part question, and the right window reloads\nas soon as the first fetch appears, while the answer is still being built.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 96.63,
   "toSeconds": 107.86
  },
  {
   "text": "After the reload the right window replays the whole turn from the server:\nevery fetched result and the answer, in order, once each.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 107.86,
   "toSeconds": 119.24
  },
  {
   "text": "Reconnect: the right window goes offline while the left buyer keeps posting.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 119.24,
   "toSeconds": 138.15
  },
  {
   "text": "Back online: the right window replays from its saved cursor. Both missed messages arrive once each, in order.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 138.15,
   "toSeconds": 149.5
  },
  {
   "text": "The other chain: the right window signs out and signs in as a Valley Home Goods buyer.\nST-4013 is Valley's own store, so Valley gets its assortment: the same store Northside was told does not exist.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · #supply-planning · RIGHT: VALLEY BUYER 1 · #range-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 149.5,
   "toSeconds": 163.58
  },
  {
   "text": "Every claim in this video is also checked automatically against the deployed stack.\nResults, raw WebSocket frames and database comparisons: qa_evidence/runs in the repository.",
   "cast": "LEFT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 1 · RIGHT: NORTHSIDE BUYER 2 · #supply-planning",
   "fromSeconds": 163.58,
   "toSeconds": 174.95
  }
 ],
